   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x \\) and \\( dv = e^{x} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = dx \\) and \\( v = e^{x} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Exp",
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[x e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} - \\int_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} e^{x} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{0}^{\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}} e^{x} \\, dx = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - \\left(1\\right) = -1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
